<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Relations Q7 - Which equation is one-to-many</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Which of the following equations, relating \(x\) (the input) to \(y\) (the output), represents a one-to-many relation?</p>
<div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A relation is <strong>one-to-many</strong> when some input has more than one output, but no output is shared by two different inputs. For each equation, ask whether one value of \(x\) can give more than one value of \(y\), and whether two values of \(x\) can give the same \(y\).</p>
<p>For \(y = 3x - 5\), each \(x\) gives exactly one \(y\), and different \(x\) values give different \(y\) values. This is one-to-one.</p>
<p>For \(y = x^3\), each \(x\) gives one \(y\), and different \(x\) values give different cubes. This is also one-to-one.</p>
<p>For \(y = |x|\), each \(x\) gives one \(y\), but \(x = 2\) and \(x = -2\) both give \(y = 2\). This is many-to-one.</p>
<p>For \(y^2 = x\), the input \(x = 4\) gives \(y = 2\) and \(y = -2\), so one input has two outputs. Each output \(y\) comes from only one input, \(x = y^2\), so no output is shared. This is one-to-many. The correct answer is B.</p>
<p>Compare the circle \(x^2 + y^2 = 9\). There \(x = 0\) gives \(y = \pm 3\), and \(x = 3\) and \(x = -3\) both give \(y = 0\), so the circle is many-to-many rather than one-to-many.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
